WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:10.090
We come together today before
all that we hold sacred,

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:13.500
and all that makes
us truly human,

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.202
and we ask for a blessing.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:24.210
May we untie the
deep knots of racism.

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:30.560
May we unfurl a new
banner of freedom.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:33.420
May we speak the truth
so boldly that we

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:38.010
shake the seats of power.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:46.740
May we listen so bravely that
our own hearts are shaken free.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:50.440
May we find strength in
community as we break bread

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:57.390
together And as we go
forth from this place

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:01.050
may we take hold of the
precious strands of history

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:06.310
that are our own lives,
so that together, we

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:12.590
may bend the arc of our
time closer and closer

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:16.690
to the great dream of justice.

00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:18.820
Amen.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:21.320
[APPLAUSE]

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:29.550
Thank you for the blessing.

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:31.406
Thank you all for coming today.

00:01:31.406 --> 00:01:33.280
I hope you've enjoyed
this morning's program.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.720
It has been a
wonderful event, which

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:39.870
I hope has inspired you not only
to remember Dr. King's words,

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.940
but to act upon them.

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:44.470
Now we invite you to stay
for the delicious lunch.

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:50.520
[APPLAUSE]

